  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Warning issued October 24 at 1:17PM MDT until October 24 at 3:30PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.

* WHERE...Northwestern Valencia County in central New Mexico...
Northeastern Cibola County in west central New Mexico...

* WHEN...Until 330 PM MDT.

* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying
and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 117 PM MDT, emergency management reported continued flooding
in Cubero and Laguna areas due to thunderstorms. Flooding is
already occurring. Radar estimates 3 to 6 inches of rain have
fallen over the area within the last 3 days.
- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the
warned area. Flooding is occurring along the Rio San Jose.
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Grants, Laguna Pueblo, New Laguna, Cubero, Mesita, San Fidel,
Skyline-Ganipa, McCartys, Paraje and Seama.
- http://www.weather.gov/abq/EmergencyPrepFlood</Snippet>
