  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Warning issued October 24 at 11:54AM MDT until October 25 at 12:20PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning continues for the following rivers in New
Mexico...

Animas River At Farmington affecting San Juan County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...Animas River at Farmington.

* WHEN...Until Sunday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...At 12.0 feet, The riverwalk area in Farmington is flooded
and should be avoided. Water levels have not been this high since
the flood of 1927.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 10:30 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 11.5 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 9.0 feet.
- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending
at 10:30 AM MDT Saturday was 11.6 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to remain near a crest of 11.5
feet through this afternoon. It will then fall below flood stage
just after midnight tonight.
- Flood stage is 10.0 feet.
- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 11.0
feet on 05/14/1941.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
   <ExtendedData>
    <Data name="ext_event">
     <value>Flood Warning</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_severity">
     <value>Severe</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_urgency">
     <value>Immediate</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_certainty">
     <value>Observed</value>
    </Data>
    <Data name="ext_effective">
     <value>2026-10-24T11:54:00-06:00</value>
