  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Warning issued October 24 at 11:45AM MDT until October 26 at 3:07AM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in New
Mexico...

San Juan River At Shiprock affecting San Juan County.

* WHAT...Major flooding is occurring and major flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...San Juan River at Shiprock.

* WHEN...Until late Sunday night.

* IMPACTS...Catastrophic flooding of the San Juan River at and near
Shiprock will continue today.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 4:00 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 21.2 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 13.5 feet.
- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending
at 4:00 AM MDT Saturday was 21.2 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to continue above flood stage
through tomorrow afternoon and continue rising to 23.0 feet this
afternoon.
- Flood stage is 15.5 feet.
- Flood History...this is the highest river stage on record.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
