    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The National Weather Service in Albuquerque has issued a Flood
Warning for the following rivers in New Mexico...

Rio Chama Above Abiquiu affecting Rio Arriba County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...Rio Chama above Abiquiu.

* WHEN...From this evening to late Sunday night.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 8:00 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 10.1 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 10.2 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage this
evening to a crest of 11.4 feet just after midnight tonight. It
will then fall below flood stage early tomorrow afternoon.
- Flood stage is 11.0 feet.
- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 10.8
feet on 05/09/2009.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
