   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...Forecast flooding changed from Minor to Moderate severity and
increased in duration for the following rivers in New Mexico...

Rio Chama Below Chamita affecting Rio Arriba County.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and moderate flooding is
forecast.

* WHERE...Rio Chama below Chamita.

* WHEN...Until Monday morning.

* IMPACTS...At 8.0 feet, Properties along the Rio Chama and southern
reach of the Rio Ojo Caliente are flooded.  Private roadways within
several hundred yards of the river are impassable.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 8:00 AM MDT Saturday the stage was 6.8 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 5.5 feet.
- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending
at 8:00 AM MDT Saturday was 7.6 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 8.1 feet
this evening. It will then fall below flood stage late tomorrow
evening.
- Flood stage is 6.0 feet.
- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 8.0
feet on 08/09/1967.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
