  <Placemark>
   <name>Flood Warning issued October 23 at 11:21PM MDT until October 24 at 3:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>...The Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in
Colorado...

San Juan River at Pagosa Springs affecting Archuleta County.

For the San Juan River...including Pagosa Springs...Major flooding is
forecast.

* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.

* WHERE...San Juan River at Pagosa Springs.

* WHEN...Until Saturday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...At 11.0 feet, Inundation of River Center Park and water
will approach the shopping complexes adjacent to the park, north of
East Pagosa Street. Water spreads across the backyards of homes
along Hermosa Street and inundation of the bike path adjacent to
the river can be expected.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 11:00 PM MDT Friday the stage was 11.4 feet.
- Bankfull stage is 8.5 feet.
- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending
at 11:00 PM MDT Friday was 15.0 feet.
- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage just
after midnight tonight and continue falling to 6.0 feet Wednesday
evening.
- Flood stage is 10.5 feet.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
