   <name>Flood Warning issued October 23 at 3:46PM MDT until October 26 at 9:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO</name>
   <styleUrl>#sev_severe</styleUrl>
   <Style>
    <BalloonStyle />
   </Style>
   <Snippet>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is ongoing

* WHERE...Western Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...
Southern San Juan County in southeastern Utah...

* WHEN...Until 900 AM MDT Monday.

* IMPACTS...Flooding along San Juan River is occurring. Low-water
crossing are inundated with water and may not be passable. The
river is running fast and high. Do not attempt to cross.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 342 PM MDT, The San Juan River is forecast to crest tonight
around midnight between Bluff and Mexican Hat. A second rise and
higher crest is forecast along the San Juan River, peaking at
Mexican Hat Sunday Monday.
- This includes the following streams and drainages...
San Juan River
- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Mexican Hat, Tselakai Dezza, Bluff, Halchita, Montezuma Creek and
Aneth.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood</Snippet>
